412	/**
413	 * ----------------------------------------------------------
414	 * [STRATEGY_MERGE] Merge properties or erase all properties:
415	 *
416	 * Based on the fact that the existing zr element probably is reused, we now consider whether
417	 * merge or erase all properties to the existing elements.
418	 * That is, if a certain props is not specified in the latest return of `renderItem`:
419	 * + "Merge" means that do not modify the value on the existing element.
420	 * + "Erase all" means that use a default value to the existing element.
421	 *
422	 * "Merge" might bring some unexpected state retaining for users and "erase all" seems to be
423	 * more safe. "erase all" forces users to specify all of the props each time, which is recommended
424	 * in most cases.
425	 * But "erase all" theoretically disables the chance of performance optimization (e.g., just
426	 * generete shape and style at the first time rather than always do that).
427	 * So we still use "merge" rather than "erase all". If users need "erase all", they can
428	 * simply always set all of the props each time.
429	 * Some "object-like" config like `textConfig`, `textContent`, `style` which are not needed for
430	 * every element, so we replace them only when users specify them. And that is a total replace.
431	 *
432	 * TODO: There is no hint of 'isFirst' to users. So the performance enhancement cannot be
433	 * performed yet. Consider the case:
434	 * (1) setOption to "mergeChildren" with a smaller children count
435	 * (2) Use dataZoom to make an item disappear.
436	 * (3) User dataZoom to make the item display again. At that time, renderItem need to return the
437	 * full option rather than partial option to recreate the element.
438	 *
439	 * ----------------------------------------------
440	 * [STRATEGY_NULL] `hasOwnProperty` or `== null`:
441	 *
442	 * Ditinguishing "own property" probably bring little trouble to user when make el options.
443	 * So we  trade a {xx: null} or {xx: undefined} as "not specified" if possible rather than
444	 * "set them to null/undefined". In most cases, props can not be cleared. Some typicall
445	 * clearable props like `style`/`textConfig`/`textContent` we enable `false` to means
446	 * "clear". In some other special cases that the prop is able to set as null/undefined,
447	 * but not suitable to use `false`, `hasOwnProperty` is checked.
448	 *
449	 * ---------------------------------------------
450	 * [STRATEGY_TRANSITION] The rule of transition:
451	 * + For props on the root level of a element:
452	 *      If there is no `transition` specified, tansform props will be transitioned by default,
453	 *      which is the same as the previous setting in echarts4 and suitable for the scenario
454	 *      of dataZoom change.
455	 *      If `transition` specified, only the specified props will be transitioned.
456	 * + For props in `shape` and `style`:
457	 *      Only props specified in `transition` will be transitioned.
458	 * + Break:
459	 *      Since ec5, do not make transition to shape by default, because it might result in
460	 *      performance issue (especially `points` of polygon) and do not necessary in most cases.
461	 *
462	 * @return if `isMorphTo`, return `allPropsFinal`.
463	 */
464	
465	interface InnerCustomZRPathOptionStyle extends PathStyleProps {
466	    __decalPattern: PatternObject
467	}
